On Thu, May 2, 2013 at 8:23 PM, John E Clifford <kali9putra@yahoo.com>wrote:

> But you seem to have answered this question.  As xorxes notes, our formula
> 'lo ca me mi' or whatever, clearly indicates a temporally segmented mi,
> 'mi' alone leaves the matter open.  So how do we speak of the perduring mi?
>
